      "message": "This deviates from our desired behavior. It is telling CRAS to remove addr when `connectet_profiles.is_empty()`.\n\nWhat we want instead is to ask CRAS to remove addr when \"any of HFP/A2DP\" is dropped.(AVRCP wasn\u0027t taken into consideration in the removal logic though)\nThe background is that, for example, when HFP is removed the headset is very likely in a bad state that even A2DP is unstable to stream. Therefore we need to ask CRAS to stop showing this headset in the settings to user.",
